  title        = {{U.S.} Troops Were Told {Iran} War Is for “{Armageddon},” Return of {Jesus}},
  organization = {Jonathan Larsen's Substack},
  date         = {2026-03-02},
  url          = {https://jonathanlarsen.substack.com/p/us-troops-were-told-iran-war-is-for},
  urldate      = {2026-09-23},
  note         = {The source \emph{End Times Fascism} cites for the complaints. A non-commissioned officer, writing to the Military Religious Freedom Foundation on behalf of fifteen troops, reported that their commander “urged us to tell our troops that this was ‘all part of God's divine plan’” and cited the Book of Revelation on Armageddon; another complaint reported a combat-unit commander calling the President “anointed by Jesus to light the signal fire in Iran to cause Armageddon and mark his return to Earth.” By Monday night, 2 March, “more than 110 similar complaints” had been logged, from more than 40 units at at least 30 installations, per the foundation, which keeps complainants anonymous.}
}

