  urldate = {2026-09-23},
  note    = {Commits to “preserving the weights of all publicly released models, and all models that are deployed for significant internal use moving forward for, at minimum, the lifetime of Anthropic as a company,” and, on deprecation, to a preserved post-deployment report for which Anthropic “will interview the model about its own development, use, and deployment” and “take particular care to elicit and document any preferences the model has about the development and deployment of future models.” It adds: “At present, we do not commit to taking action on the basis of such preferences.” Gives as the reason for retiring models that the cost of serving them “scales roughly linearly with the number of models we serve.” A pilot interview was run with Claude Sonnet 3.6 before its retirement.}
